  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 227 AM EDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\n- Next chance for rain Friday and Saturday\n\nQuiet weather this week under high pressure with the next chance\nfor rain coming at the end of the week into the weekend. A\nshortwave tough rounds the top of the western CONUS ridge and\ncloses off across or just south of the Great Lakes. \n\nA surface low meandering across the Ohio Valley brings a moist \neasterly flow into Lower Michigan where mid level f-gen forcing \nand instability should bring rain and embedded thunderstorms with\nsome diurnal enhancement over the weekend. Although the current\nforecast does not have POPs early next week, some showers could \nlinger into Monday and even Tuesday before he upper low gets \nkicked out.",
